  "gold_meta": {
    "corpus": "McGuffey Third Reader (PG#14766, public domain), lessons L04,L05,L07,L08,L09,L10,L12 (clean narrative prose; L06 title-only + L11 blacksmith poem excluded).",
    "annotator": "exp_dev single-annotator (glass-box agent), 2026-07-19",
    "independence": "Annotated by reading the raw McGuffey sentence text and writing the TRUE argument structure per sentence. The point of this gold is to mark, per verb-INSTANCE, whether it takes a direct affected/created/perceived PATIENT (pos) or takes NO direct patient (nopat: intransitive-motion / cognition-clausal / oblique-perception / report / copular / aspectual). The reader's extraction output was used ONLY to key which sentence-ids exist; the pos/nopat argument-structure judgments are the annotator's own reading of the text (ground truth), independent of what the reader extracted. Keyed to deterministic sentence ids (split_sents on the lessons).",
    "standard": "pos relation = (v_lemma, agent_head, patient_head) where an AGENT acts on / creates / perceives a distinct PATIENT/THEME ENTITY. Heads are surface tokens (pronouns kept). nopat instance = (v_lemma, agent_head) for a verb occurrence that licenses NO direct patient: intransitive self-motion (come/go/sit/stand/fall/run/walk/spring/leap/creep/swim), cognition/clausal-complement (think/know/wonder/mean/wish/hope/believe/see-that/find-that/fear/suppose/choose/prefer/intend/learn), oblique/perception-AT (look-at/tread-on/struggle-against/meddle-with/fire-on/reach-for/inquire-about), report/speech (say/said/cry[exclaim]/ask/answer/retort/tell[recipient+clause]/call[summon]/exclaim/speak), aspectual (begin/commence/try/continue-of-motion), copular/light-idiom (do-no-harm/get-finished). A verb-instance is in EXACTLY one of pos or nopat (or absent if not annotated). EXCLUDED entirely (neither): passives with no expressed agent, bare copulas, embedded infinitive objects, gerund-internal objects, quantifier-only 'nothing/nobody' patients, ambiguous idioms.",
    "usage": "PRIMARY precision/recall over pos (v_lemma, patient) patient-level. SUBCAT TRUE-NEGATIVE: over nopat verb-instances the reader mis-attached a patient to, does an arm SUPPRESS the wrong patient (correct) vs keep it (subcat FP). WITHIN-FRAME FP: reader keeps a wrong patient on a verb whose pos set is non-empty. refs = agent coref surfaces for the lenient-agent triple metric only.",
    "caveat": "SINGLE-ANNOTATOR gold; the pos-vs-nopat boundary involves judgment calls (rub-against/knit-forehead/nod-head counted as pos contact/body-part per the sibling v1 gold convention; look-at/tread-on/struggle-against counted nopat oblique). Full gold + full reader output + all matches are reported in metrics so a VET can independently re-annotate the same sentences and recompute.",
    "characters": "Herbert(he/his/him), Joe(he/him), papa/Mr.Rose(he), Hetty(she/her), pussy=cat(she/her/it), Charles(he/him), James(he/him), Frank(he/him), the gardener(he), mother/mamma(she/her), father(he), the castle/block/kite/hut(it)."
  },
